UgzZ3P8LDYtyQB4QgEZ4AaABAg,,False,@lseals1430,"Seokjin is the most critically- acclaimed vocalist in BTS. He has two personal articles by Grammy and he is called Grammy's Silver Voice"". Silver-voiced means having a clear, sweet voice like the sound of a silver musical instrument.

Korean Grammy equivalent - KMA - the critics of it called Jin's voice basically the reason Fake Love was chosen as the Song Of The Year.

MTV called him the Nation's Vocalist!

NME called his falsetto in Dionysus the best moment of MOTS album.

World Music Awards comparing his singing in the self-composed track ""Tonight"" to Mariah Carey.

Time Magazine also singled out Jin's voice ""Jin’s bright tone, in particular, shines in delivering the bittersweet emotions of wrestling between holding on and letting go, the internal struggle described by the lyrics.""
         -TIME magazine on 'Let Go'

American musical director and brilliant pianist, James Carl Osorio also called Jin ""a true belting king"" for demonstrating the ""technique-driven vocals"" and even while dancing hitting every high note and belting them with power and ease.

Isak Choi in the Big issue Magazine got deeply impressed by Jin as a person and artist while doing his research. He
called Jin's vocals the heart of BTS's music. When the voices of four vocalists unite to rush to the climax of the song, his voice serves as the engine that further spikes the upsurge"".

Jin's solo song ""Moon"" is the only BTS song that made it to to the Top 5 in Rolling Stone's 75 Greatest Boyband Songs of All Time.

Music critic Doheon Kim names ""Epiphany"" as one of BTS's best songs and praises Jin's solo music.

The list goes on...

Seokjin's voice covers the range of all members from the low notes to the highest belting ones and got BTS's songs lots of attention from critics and even nominations.",649,2021-07-28T22:14:07Z,2021-08-03T23:37:31Z
